{"name":"Sebright Chicken","hex":"#bd5701","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chicken","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A domesticated subspecies of red junglefowl (Gallus gallus domesticus).","The meat from this bird eaten as food."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cowardly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chicken"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sebright chicken","blocks":[{"text":"The Sebright is a British breed of bantam chicken. It is a true bantam – a miniature bird with no corresponding large version – and is one of the oldest recorded British bantam breeds. It is named after Sir John Saunders Sebright, who created it as an ornamental breed by selective breeding in the early nineteenth century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Sebright_Gold_Dor%C3%A9.jpg/330px-Sebright_Gold_Dor%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebright_chicken","wikidata":"Q1087454"},{"title":"Chicken","blocks":[{"text":"The chicken is the domesticated form of the red junglefowl, originally native to Southeast Asia. It was first domesticated around 8,000 years ago and is one of the most common and widespread domesticated animals in the world. Chickens are primarily kept for their meat and eggs, though they are also kept as pets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg/330px-Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken","wikidata":"Q780"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Silver_Sebright_hen.jpg/500px-Silver_Sebright_hen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Silver_Sebright_hen.jpg/500px-Silver_Se